.TH BIBLIA-ELIM-NAV "1" "@XIPHOS_RELEASE_DATE@" "Ministerios Elim @PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH "NAME"
biblia-elim\-nav \- Navigating Ministerios Elim to a verse reference
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBbiblia-elim-nav\fR \s-1URL\s0

.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.B biblia-elim-nav
is a command line utility which induce Ministerios Elim to react to a \s-1URL\s0 request
using dbus.  Invoke it as e.g. 'biblia-elim-nav sword://ESV/Gen.1.1'. Normal
use is that it's used as your desktop environment's handler for
sword:// URLs.  If dbus access attempt fails, it concludes that Ministerios Elim
is not running and starts a new Ministerios Elim with that \s-1URL. \s0 With this, you
can click URLs of that sort in web pages and so forth, and Ministerios Elim will
be navigated for you.  The dbus interface also supports a search
interface, used by bibledit.

.SH "BUGS"
Please report bugs online at: https://github.com/OmarGonD/biblia-elim/issues

.SH "AUTHOR"
.B biblia-elim-nav
is maintained by the Ministerios Elim contributors.
.PP
